This study aims to determine the structural, optical, and electrical properties of PVA/PVP hybrid matrix nanocomposites incorporating graphene nanoplatelets (GnPs). The primary objective is to investigate the effect of different GnP concentrations (0.00, 1.19, 2.40, 3.63, 4.88, and 6.16 vol%) on the performance of the hybrid nanocomposites and to evaluate their potential for optical energy storage devices and optoelectronic applications. Electrical conductivity measurements demonstrated a significant enhancement in conductivity with increasing GnP content. The optical bandgap ( E g ) exhibited a decreasing trend, while the Urbach energy ( E u \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
